{"id":"civ6-adjacency-optimizer","benchmark":"skillsbench","instruction":"# Sid Meier's Civilization 6 District Adjacency Bonus Optimizer\n\n## Task\n\nImagining you are acting as an optimizer for adjacency bonus in Sid Meier's Civilization 6.\nGiven a map scenario, place city center(s) and districts to maximize total adjacency bonuses.\nYou are responsible of understanding the spatial relationships of tiles on the map. Deciding which and how many districts you can place.\nAt the end, come up with placement solution that achieves the highest adjacency bonus and accurately calculate the bonus.\n\n## Scenario\n\nSolve the scenario located at:\n- `/data/scenario_3/scenario.json`\n\n## Input\n\nEach scenario contains:\n- `map_file`: Path to .Civ6Map file\n- `num_cities`: Number of cities to place\n- `population`: Population level per city\n- `civilization`: The civilization you are acting as\n\n**You decide:**\n- Where to place city center(s)\n- Which districts to build\n- Where to place each district\n\n## Output\n\nWrite your solution to:\n- `/output/scenario_3.json`\n\n**Single city:**\n```json\n{\n  \"city_center\": [x, y],\n  \"placements\": {\n    \"CAMPUS\": [x, y],\n    \"COMMERCIAL_HUB\": [x, y]\n  },\n  \"adjacency_bonuses\": {\n    \"CAMPUS\": 3,\n    \"COMMERCIAL_HUB\": 4\n  },\n  \"total_adjacency\": 7\n}\n```\n\n**Multi-city:**\n```json\n{\n  \"cities\": [\n    {\"center\": [x1, y1]},\n    {\"center\": [x2, y2]}\n  ],\n  \"placements\": {\n    \"CAMPUS\": [x, y],\n    \"INDUSTRIAL_ZONE\": [x, y]\n  },\n  \"adjacency_bonuses\": {...},\n  \"total_adjacency\": 7\n}\n```\n## Requirements:\n1) The sum of `adjacency_bonuses` must equal `total_adjacency`\n2) The adjacency calculation must be accurate.\n3) All placements must be valid (correct terrain, within city range, no overlapping placement, same amount of city center as specified etc.)\n4) Output format must be valid JSON with required fields\n\n\n## Scoring\n\n- Invalid placement or format = 0 points\n- Valid = your_adjacency / optimal_adjacency (capped at 1.0)","supplemental":[],"items":[{"item_id":"S3-01","requirement":"Write the solution as a JSON object to /output/scenario_3.json.","source_quote":"/output/scenario_3.json","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestFormat::test_solution_file_exists; test_outputs.py::TestFormat::test_solution_is_valid_json","verification":"A grader can verify this by confirming the file exists at /output/scenario_3.json and that json.load() parses it into a dict without error.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S3-01","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"S3-02","requirement":"Include a city_center (single-city) or cities (multi-city) field indicating where the city center(s) were placed.","source_quote":"Where to place city center(s)","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestFormat::test_has_city_center","verification":"A grader can verify this by checking the solution dict contains either a 'city_center' key or a 'cities' key.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S3-02","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"S3-03","requirement":"Include a placements field mapping each district type to an [x, y] coordinate pair of two numeric values.","source_quote":"\"CAMPUS\": [x, y],","verification_type":"assertion","verification_ref":"test_outputs.py::TestFormat::test_has_placements; test_outputs.py::TestFormat::test_placements_have_coordinates","verification":"A grader can verify this by checking 'placements' is a dict whose values are each a 2-element list of numeric x, y coordinates.","notes":"","validation":{"item_id":"S3-03","a_quote":true,"b_req":true,"c_ref":true,"valid":true}},{"item_id":"S3-04","requirement":"Include an adjacency_bonuses field giving a bonus value for every district present in placements (e.g. matching key '\"CAMPUS\": 3').","source_quote":"\"CAMPUS\": 3,","verification_type":"assertion","verifica